KG42.register("edges-dbdfcf017bc0e793ba5ad25f",{"id":"S-1d80e4a314913060","source":"COMP-10be07664c6496b7","type":"links","target":"COMP-5931b196ea5babe4","evidence_class":"S","scientific_acceptance":false,"relation_scope":"original_occurrence_pair_only","internal_to_parent":false,"paper_ids":["07-nash_bargaining"],"assertions":[{"id":"07-nash_bargaining::v141-c-R002::E::v141-c-R002-E001","paper":"07-nash_bargaining","rule_id":"v141-c-R002","rule_ref":"07-nash_bargaining::v141-c-R002","record":{"edge_id":"v141-c-R002-E001","source":"coordination.local_operator","target":"clearing.social_welfare","type":"links","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R002-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E17","v141-b-g02-E35","v141-b-g02-E37"]},"evidence_class":"S","provenance_gate":"direct_C_edge_with_constraint_and_source_excerpt","scientific_acceptance":false,"accepted_constraint_ids":["v141-c-R002-C001"],"held_constraint_ids":[],"semantic_review_status":"supported","source":"COMP-10be07664c6496b7","target":"COMP-5931b196ea5babe4","source_occurrence_id":"07-nash_bargaining::v141-c-R002::V::coordination.local_operator","target_occurrence_id":"07-nash_bargaining::v141-c-R002::V::clearing.social_welfare","source_unit_id":"07-nash_bargaining::v141-a-M01::coordination.local_operator","target_unit_id":"07-nash_bargaining::v141-a-M01::clearing.social_welfare","omega":{"market_type":"DEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"clearing","context_text":"Problem P1 over all interconnected microgrids in M. | Step 1 of Algorithm 1, solving P1 for the interconnected-microgrid system. | The microgrids in trading set M′.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E16","v141-b-g02-E17","v141-b-g02-E18","v141-b-g02-E35","v141-b-g02-E37"]},"active":true,"source_signature":"5a3d21c746828b368ee96063892bafa4588d8367b6d968a48361481d0ea04b34","relation_scope":"original_occurrence_pair_only","internal_to_parent":false,"source_science":{"mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","source_definition":"Virtual clearing house receives P1 energy schedules and P2 payments and updates auxiliary/dual signals. Energy and payment stages remain separate objects.","target_definition":"Economic objective and its applicability in this mechanism: P1 first minimizes interconnected microgrids total operating cost and fixes bilateral energy; P2 maximizes the product of net gains of the active trading set through payment bargaining.","constraints":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R002-C001","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"The virtual clearing house coordinates the higher-level updates in the distributed solution of P1's social operating-cost minimization; microgrids solve the lower-level problems. Scope: Step 1 of Algorithm 1, solving P1 for the interconnected-microgrid system.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["coordination.local_operator","clearing.social_welfare"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E17","v141-b-g02-E35","v141-b-g02-E37"]}],"evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E17","location":{"location_id":"src-7e85444402-p06-c2r2__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":6,"printed_page":"2652","section":"IV. PROBLEM ANALYSIS","anchor_text":"BP can be decomposed into two sequential subproblems on energy d- trading & scheduling and trading p","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-06.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"Theorem 1: The energy-trading bargaining problem NBP can be decomposed into two sequential subproblems on energy trading & scheduling and trading payment, denoted as P1 and P2, respectively. In the first step, we solve a social operating cost minimization problem P1 for the interconnected-microgrids system, which yields the optimal energy scheduling and energy trading for all microgrids. Those microgrids that trade energy with other microgrids form the set M′. In the second step, microgrids in set M′ bargain with each other to determine the energy-trading payments in P2."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E35","location":{"location_id":"src-7e85444402-p08-c2r1__v141-a-M01-activation","page":8,"printed_page":"2654","section":"V.C Algorithm Design and Implementation","anchor_text":"IEEE TRANSACTIONS ON SMART GRID, VOL. 9, NO. 4, JULY 2018 Algorithm 1 Distributed Algorithm Solving ","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-08.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"Algorithm 1 Distributed Algorithm Solving P1 and P2\n1: Step 1: solve Problem P1.\n2: Initialization: iteration index k = 1, error tolerance ϵ1 > 0, stepsize ρ1(0) = 1, and initial multipliers λ(0) = 0.\n3: repeat\n4: At k-th iteration,\n5: Lower Level Problem: Microgrid i solves Problem P1-MGi based on the current value of dual variables λ(k);\n6: Higher Level Problem: The virtual clearing house makes update according to (21) and (22).\n7: Update iteration index k = k + 1;\n8: until terminal condition is satisfied ...\n9: Step 2: solve Problem P2.\n10: Initialization: iteration index k = 1, error tolerance ϵ2 > 0, stepsize ρ2(0) = 1, and initial multipliers γ(0) = 0.\n11: repeat\n12: At k-th iteration,\n13: Lower Level Problem: Microgrid i solves Problem P2-MGi based on the current value of dual variables γ(k);\n14: Higher Level Problem: The virtual clearing house makes updates according to the rules in (25) and (26).\n15: Update iteration index k = k + 1;\n16: until terminal condition is satisfied ...\n17: end"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E37","location":{"location_id":"src-7e85444402-p08-c2r4__v141-a-M01-activation","page":8,"printed_page":"2654","section":"V.C Algorithm Design and Implementation","anchor_text":"To implement the solution method for solving the energy trading and payment problems P1 and P2, we d","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-08.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"We introduce the concept of virtual clearing house for solving the higher level problem. The virtual clearing house is a communication and computing module, which provides clearing service of energy trading and payment for all the microgrids. At the beginning of each daily operation, the virtual clearing house updates the auxiliary and dual variables according to (21), (22) and (25), (26), and broadcasts to all participating microgrids when solving P1 and P2, respectively. All the participating microgrids concurrently solve P1-MGi and P2-MGi and report their energy trading schedules and payments to the virtual clearing house."}],"omega":{"market_type":"DEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"clearing","context_text":"Problem P1 over all interconnected microgrids in M. | Step 1 of Algorithm 1, solving P1 for the interconnected-microgrid system. | The microgrids in trading set M′.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E16","v141-b-g02-E17","v141-b-g02-E18","v141-b-g02-E35","v141-b-g02-E37"]},"source_record":{"edge_id":"v141-c-R002-E001","source":"coordination.local_operator","target":"clearing.social_welfare","type":"links","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R002-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E17","v141-b-g02-E35","v141-b-g02-E37"]},"paper_scope_note":"Distinguish the interfaces of P1 dispatch, P2 payment, the actual transaction set, and the clearing institution; the same clearing institution does not mean that the variables of P1 and P2 can be merged."}}],"assertion_ids":["07-nash_bargaining::v141-c-R002::E::v141-c-R002-E001"]});
